A kretprobe fires two handlers: entry_handler before the function runs, and
handler (the return handler) after it returns.
Use the per-instance data field (inst->data) to pass state between them.
In the entry handler, set intercepted = true and store the result.
In the return handler, call regs_set_return_value to override the syscall return
code.
Parse the command by finding the first dot after "rklings."
in the basename.
